course: dictionary
lesson: 3824
title: One word, many forms
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «form» can mean several things, so context tells you which meaning to use. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: In «a cloud in the form of a rabbit», form means shape. In «ice is a form of water», form means a kind or type. Both are nouns, and the words around them show which meaning fits.
explain: In «ice forms on the pond», form is a verb meaning to make or take shape. Check by swapping in your meaning: «ice takes shape on the pond» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: In «fill in a form», a form is a paper or online page with spaces for information. In the UK, your form is also your class at school, so «my form teacher» means the teacher of your class.
fact: Form can be a noun (a form, forms) or a verb (to form, forming).
fact: Form can mean a shape, a kind, a paper to fill in, a school class in the UK, or to make something.
fact: In grammar, a form is one version of a word: «ran» is a form of «run».
fact: «Pronouns» come in two forms: subject forms do the action, like «I» and «we», and object forms receive it, like «me» and «us».
fact: Water can be found in three forms: solid, liquid and gas.
exercise: «A cloud in the form of a rabbit drifted past.» What does form mean here? | A school class | To make something | A paper to fill in | *A shape
exercise: «Ice forms on the pond in winter.» What does forms mean here? | Fills in | Is a kind of water | Goes away | *Makes or takes shape
exercise: In «ran is a form of run», what is ran? | *A version of the word run | A paper to fill in | A kind of ice | A school class
test: «Gritters spread salt before a frost, so ice forms less easily.» What does forms mean here? | Is a type of salt | *Takes shape | Fills in a page | Melts away quickly
test: Mum says, «Fill in this form for the school trip.» What is the form? | A version of a word | *A paper with spaces for information | A shape | A class at school
exam: «Form» in «Sam and I went» versus «Mum gave sweets to Ben and me» shows that pronouns come in two forms; which word is the object form? | we | they | *me | I
